sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 42 µm on Gasterosteus doryssus_mid (Truckee Fm, 10.01 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 86.8/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 closes the three Pass 1 remediations. Du scaled by 0.9 and 1.1 moves λ from 39.80 µm to 44.02 µm around the calibrated 41.94 µm. The unguided activator GIF scores CV 58.1; the specimen-registered growth GIF (12 frames, 640×480) scores CV 92.3. The darkest 40% of the plate (bone) has radial KS 0.333 against the render; the sediment complement has KS 0.542. Dispersion Pearson r remains 0.9897, RMSE 0.070. Early/mid/late wavelengths remain 32.14 / 41.94 / 56.90 µm at 10.02 / 10.01 / 9.99 Ma. Overall 86.8/100. Nanopubs are unsigned: ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is absent. Overall 86.8/100 (faithfulness 86.1, reproducibility 88.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 91, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/gasterosteus_doryssus_mid_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/gif, 2323139 B, 640×480 px, 12 frames, artifact_sha256 101ffda1755cf4e1742f15b040a2a2c4e8e46fafa1f20a7ecbbcb9a7e060dc44 (sha256 101ffda1755cf4e1742f15b040a2a2c4e8e46fafa1f20a7ecbbcb9a7e060dc44), spec_fingerprint dc4c1601bb00a6d80d4baed16fe77c8243511e825b49d7d785e454e5f8378e0b. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: dc4c1601bb00a6d80d4baed16fe77c8243511e825b49d7d785e454e5f8378e0b; artifact_sha256: 101ffda1755cf4e1742f15b040a2a2c4e8e46fafa1f20a7ecbbcb9a7e060dc44; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/gasterosteus_doryssus_mid_turing_wavelength_s0/gasterosteus_doryssus_mid_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=38c0a5455a7e482a..., datasets/gasterosteus_doryssus_mid_turing_wavelength_s0/gasterosteus_doryssus_mid_turing_wavelength_s0_specimen.jpg=a1d587e4264868ea...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion: a critical wavenumber selected by diffusion and reaction rates. | Kondo & Asai 1995: reaction-diffusion waves set pigment spacing on fish skin. | Bell & Haglund 1982 and Hunt, Bell & Travis 2008: directional pelvic reduction in Truckee Fm G. doryssus. | Shapiro et al. 2004 and Chan et al. 2010: extant pelvic reduction maps to a Pitx1 enhancer deletion. | Voje, Bell & Stuart 2022: CC BY 4.0 plate of weakly and strongly armored G. doryssus morphs.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg Jacobian at (a, b) = (0.062, 1.18), σ(k), and Du bisection onto 41.94 µm. | Chronoseries (Dv/Du, γ) = (14.2, 1.55), (18, 1), (24.8, 0.62) giving 32.14, 41.94, 56.90 µm. | Du ±10% band 39.80 / 41.94 / 44.02 µm, pure-field CV 58.1 beside registered CV 92.3, bone-mask KS.; transfer_boundary: 42 µm melanophore spacing is transferred from extant pigment-pattern RD onto a fossil that preserves bone, not chromatophores.; does_not_claim: That the centimetre-scale fossil photograph is a 42 µm histological section. | That Pitx1 was sequenced from these Miocene fish. | That the unguided stripe field reproduces the skeleton. Its CV is 58.1; the 92.3 score is the registered render.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Residual, not a failed numerical gate: no second assessor, and ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is absent so the nanopubs stay unsigned.'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.868"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, Pass 2 after R1–R3)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

